  Wait — but there's a subtlety with `_role_liveness_struck`: it suppresses when `role in state` AND struck line exists on board. But the board gets struck lines and they accumulate — an old struck line from a *previous* death episode remains forever. So if the role dies again later (new episode), state was cleared on recovery... but if it dies without recovery being observed (e.g., state popped on recovery check then re-dies), state cleared → `role in state` False → alerts. Good, that matches the rearm logic.

